Australian Product Guide — Brand Fidelity v32.5 certified presentation release
Release date: 2026-08-18
Status: CURRENT RELEASE CANDIDATE / EXACT PRODUCTION CERTIFICATION REQUIRED AFTER MERGE
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: the underlying APG application/data capability remains the maintained priority-commerce / Decision Intelligence v4.1 / Evidence & Commerce Depth v27 / Trust Infrastructure v28 / Amazon Conversion v29 stack, with Premium Brand v30, Premium Theme v31.1 and Brand Fidelity v32.5 forming the controlling presentation system once this release is merged and exact-Production certified. The architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement. v32.5 changes presentation and release controls only; it does not change product-fit logic, catalogue data, retailer ranking, affiliate weighting, account/auth behaviour, analytics consent or privacy controls.

Brand-fidelity truth: the owner-approved APG brand board is implemented as a coherent production identity rather than an approximate A-shaped logo. The current mark uses the traced four-part APG geometry and first-party responsive assets for primary horizontal, compact, APG monogram, standalone symbol, white, monochrome, favicon, app-icon and social applications. Desktop uses the full Australian Product Guide lock-up. Standard tablet/mobile widths use the APG symbol/monogram relationship, with the monogram P kept white on navy so the complete APG mark remains legible.

Colour-system truth: the controlling palette is APG Blue #2563EB, APG Navy #0F172A, APG Teal #06B6D4, APG Green #10B981, Light Grey #F1F5F9 and Slate #64748B, supported by white and accessible light/dark text tokens. Navy is used for institutional authority and deep surfaces; blue is the primary action colour; teal/green remain selective accents; white/light grey provide breathing space. Dark surfaces use white or sufficiently light foreground text rather than low-contrast navy/grey combinations.

Maintained-research highlight: the successful historical yellow treatment was recovered from APG source history rather than guessed. The MAINTAINED AUSTRALIAN RESEARCH band uses #FFD65B → #F4BB45 → #F2B348, with #E0A630/#D89C24 border tones and dark foreground treatment. The main proof text remains based on the recovered #082735 family and the independence copy is explicitly #2B4B56 at strong weight. Yellow remains a strategic trust accent rather than a primary site colour. Product/category/brand values remain data-driven from the maintained catalogue rather than hard-coded release numbers.

Scout and proof clearance: Scout remains APG's decision-assistance product and uses the APG Blue + white master symbol consistently after JavaScript initialisation. v32.2 prevents the legacy mascot overwriting the approved APG mark. v32.3 makes the fixed desktop launcher a compact 58px APG-symbol control so it cannot obscure the yellow research independence statement. Scout decision logic, structured-session continuity and zero-commercial-weight recommendation controls are unchanged.

Mobile navigation reconciliation: manual review of exact Production screenshots exposed a timing conflict between the intended v32.4 DOM reconciliation and older mobile CSS/client behaviour. Although the v32.4 assertion observed one Decision Lab and one Ask Scout in the live DOM, the captured screenshot could still show the historical visual state because `.mobile-power + .mobile-power` hid the adjacent Scout action and a later client mutation could alter the visible label after the assertion. v32.5 removes that race. The authoritative Decision Lab and Ask Scout controls are now classified server-side in SSR, visually labelled through dedicated CSS pseudo-content, assigned stable grid order before the accordion sections, and the old adjacent-control hiding rule is explicitly overridden. Any later unclassified duplicate `.mobile-power` action is hidden, while a final MutationObserver preserves the intended classes and accessible labels. The target visible hierarchy is therefore deterministically Decision Lab → Ask Scout → Popular products → Research & compare → Trust & transparency.

Catalogue and commerce truth: catalogue, retailer, Amazon and recommendation facts are verified from the live observability contract during exact-Production certification rather than copied into the interface as release constants. Affiliate participation, retailer availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Imagery truth: the governed registry continues to distinguish authorised external exact-model photography from first-party/category-correct authored decision visuals. APG does not scrape Amazon product pages, reverse-engineer image URLs, fabricate real-product photography or claim third-party imagery rights it does not hold. Authorised genuine-product image delivery remains a separate ingestion task where rights/delivery are not available.

Responsive and accessibility truth: the full v32 Production matrix continues to cover homepage, search, category, product, comparison, Decision Lab, My APG, trust/footer and Scout across desktop, tablet and mobile. v32.5 adds an additional exact-Production tablet/mobile visual gate that waits after menu opening, validates the CSS-rendered Decision Lab and Ask Scout labels, requires both controls to be visibly rendered, verifies their actual vertical order ahead of the accordion groups, rejects visible unclassified duplicate power actions, checks page width and saves dedicated menu screenshots for manual review.

Implementation history: PR #79 established v32.2 board-faithful identity and Scout/mobile corrections. PR #81 introduced v32.3 after screenshot review found residual yellow-proof contrast and Scout-clearance defects. v32.4 then introduced the first mobile Decision Lab/Ask Scout reconciliation, but manual inspection of its exact screenshot artefact correctly overruled the green timing-sensitive assertion. v32.5 is the final SSR/CSS-stable rendering correction and is not complete until its exact Production screenshot itself visually shows Decision Lab followed by Ask Scout with no duplicate.

Release verification requirement: this file is included in the same v32.5 implementation PR so the final merged GitHub main SHA can remain the exact SHA certified. Completion requires Vercel READY on the canonical domain, APG v27 Visual Certification success, APG v32 Brand Visual Certification success, APG v32.5 Mobile Visual Certification success on the same SHA, publication of both final screenshot artefacts, manual inspection of the v32.5 mobile-menu screenshot, and a clear post-release Vercel error/fatal log window.

Remaining external gaps: lawful genuine-product photography ingestion remains incomplete until an authorised delivery/right basis exists. Hosted Supabase Auth settings outside the connected writable surface, including any previously identified leaked-password-protection setting unless subsequently verified, remain separate owner/admin configuration work. Formal trade mark clearance/registration is not claimed by this release.
